# VS Code : extension "REST Client" (humao.rest-client)
# Remplacer email, password, clientId par vos valeurs (clientId = users.id = userId login)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@email = votre.email@example.com
@password = votreMotDePasse
@clientId = 27

### 1 — Login (récupérer userId = clientId)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

###
@userId = {{login.response.body.userId}}

### 2 — Lire les préférences (charger les switches React)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/alerts/{{clientId}}
Authorization: Basic {{email}} {{password}}

### 3 — Créer le référentiel (première fois, si GET 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/alerts
Authorization: Basic {{email}} {{password}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientId": {{clientId}},
  "alerteTransaction": true,
  "alerteFraude": true,
  "alerteCarte": true,
  "active": true,
  "blackList": false,
  "telephone": "0612345678"
}

### 4 — Mettre à jour UN switch (PATCH partiel)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/alerts/{{clientId}}
Authorization: Basic {{email}} {{password}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "alerteTransaction": false
}

### 5 — Sauvegarder TOUS les switches (PUT — recommandé pour l'écran paramètres)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/alerts/{{clientId}}
Authorization: Basic {{email}} {{password}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "alerteTransaction": true,
  "alerteFraude": true,
  "alerteCarte": false,
  "active": true,
  "blackList": false,
  "telephone": "0612345678"
}
